# Copy this file to .env  (cp .env.example .env)  and fill in your DEMO keys.
# The .env file stays on your machine. Never paste these values into chat,
# commits, or screenshots.
#
# How to create DEMO keys on BloFin:
#   1. Log in at blofin.com and switch to Demo Trading
#      (profile menu -> Demo Trading).
#   2. While in demo mode, open API management and create an API key.
#      It will be a demo-trading key, separate from any live key.
#   3. Permissions: READ + TRADE only. Never grant withdrawal/transfer.
#   4. You will set a passphrase when creating it — that's the third value.

BLOFIN_DEMO_API_KEY=your_key_here
BLOFIN_DEMO_API_SECRET=your_secret_here
BLOFIN_DEMO_PASSPHRASE=your_passphrase_here


# ============================================================ OANDA (FOREX)
#
# The currency venue: GBP/JPY, GBP/USD and EUR/USD. (Spot gold, XAU/USD, is
# wired but NOT tradeable on a US practice account — see step 5 below.)
# This is a PRACTICE account. It has no funding behind it and it cannot
# reach real money.
#
# HOW TO CREATE IT — about four minutes, no payment method, no approval wait.
#
#   1. Go to  https://www.oanda.com/  and click "Try a demo" / "Open a demo
#      account". (Direct link, if it still works when you read this:
#      https://www.oanda.com/apply/demo/ )
#      Give an email, a name and a password. That is the whole signup — a
#      demo account needs no ID, no funding and no approval.
#
#   2. Confirm the email, then log in to the ACCOUNT MANAGEMENT portal:
#          https://www.oanda.com/demo-account/tpa/personal_token
#      (If that link moves: log in, then "Manage API Access" / "My Services"
#      -> "Manage API Access".)
#
#   3. Click GENERATE / REVOKE to create a personal access token.
#      COPY IT IMMEDIATELY. OANDA shows it once. It is a long hex string
#      with a hyphen in the middle, like
#          1a2b3c4d5e6f...-7g8h9i0j...
#      That value goes in OANDA_API_TOKEN below.
#
#   4. On the same portal, find your ACCOUNT NUMBER. It looks like
#          101-001-1234567-001
#      A PRACTICE account always starts with 101-. A live account starts
#      with 001-. If the number you copy starts with 001-, you are on the
#      wrong account: go back and pick the demo one. The bot checks this
#      itself and refuses to start on a mismatch, but check it anyway.
#      That value goes in OANDA_ACCOUNT_ID below.
#
#   5. Put both values in your local .env, then run
#          python3 oanda_api.py --smoke
#      It confirms the token works, that the account is a practice account,
#      which instruments it can actually trade and each one's own pip size,
#      and that candles come back at every timeframe. IT PLACES NOTHING.
#
#      EXPECT XAU/USD (GOLD) TO FAIL THAT CHECK, and it is not a broken key.
#      Measured on the real account 2026-07-26: it carries 68 instruments
#      and every one is a currency pair. A US-regulated retail forex account
#      may not hold spot metals, so gold is not on it. Gold CANDLES still
#      read back fine — that endpoint is account-wide — which is exactly the
#      trap: gold looks available until an order is sent. The venue refuses
#      to trade any instrument whose spec it could not read, so it stops
#      before the order rather than after.
#
#   6. THEN PUT THE SAME TWO VALUES INTO RENDER. Keys that existed only on
#      the laptop have silently broken the cloud worker twice. In the Render
#      dashboard: the cryptobot service -> Environment -> Add Environment
#      Variable, once for each of the two names below, then Save (which
#      redeploys). The names are exactly:
#
#          OANDA_API_TOKEN
#          OANDA_ACCOUNT_ID
#
# THE SAME TWO NAMES WORK FOR LIVE. Which host they reach is decided by the
# venue name in config, not by the variable name — and the live venue
# additionally refuses to build unless CRYPTOBOT_REAL_MONEY holds the exact
# confirmation phrase. Put a PRACTICE token here. Nothing points at live.

OANDA_API_TOKEN=your_personal_access_token_here
OANDA_ACCOUNT_ID=101-001-0000000-001
